From: DogukanDG <dagtekindogukan1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:06:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Let the event log be switched off at run time

The XES log is the largest thing a run writes: 16 MB of the 23 MB a 3000-case
BPIC 2012 simulation produces, against 7 MB for the statistics a KPI pipeline
actually reads. A batch of concurrent simulations therefore spends most of its
I/O on a file nothing downstream opens, and where that write goes to a shared
network filesystem it dominates: 28 concurrent samples measured 14.8 s each,
against 10.3 s for a single sample on its own.

-Dscylla.xes=off suppresses it. Removing the plugin from plugins_list achieves
the same, but the log is what tests assert against, so the switch belongs at
run time rather than at build time.

Measured on one sample: 3.4 s to 2.6 s, 23.4 MB to 7.3 MB, KPIs unchanged.
---
 .../scylla/plugin/xeslogger/XESLogger.java    | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main/java/de/hpi/bpt/scylla/plugin/xeslogger/XESLogger.java b/src/main/java/de/hpi/bpt/scylla/plugin/xeslogger/XESLogger.java
index b5f5936..fc766f0 100644
--- a/src/main/java/de/hpi/bpt/scylla/plugin/xeslogger/XESLogger.java
+++ b/src/main/java/de/hpi/bpt/scylla/plugin/xeslogger/XESLogger.java
@@ -44,8 +44,32 @@ public class XESLogger extends OutputLoggerPluggable {
         return "XES";
     }
 
+    /**
+     * System property that suppresses the event log: {@code -Dscylla.xes=off}.
+     *
+     * The XES log is the largest thing a run writes -- 16 MB of the 23 MB a
+     * 3000-case BPIC 2012 sample produces, against 7 MB for the statistics the
+     * KPIs are actually read from. A batch of concurrent samples therefore
+     * spends most of its I/O on a file nothing downstream opens, and on a
+     * cluster that write goes to a shared network filesystem: measured, 28
+     * concurrent samples ran slower in total than a single sample on its own.
+     *
+     * Removing the plugin from plugins_list would do the same, but the log is
+     * what the plugin tests assert against, so it has to stay switchable at run
+     * time rather than at build time.
+     */
+    public static final String DISABLE_PROPERTY = "scylla.xes";
+
+    private static boolean isDisabled() {
+        return "off".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty(DISABLE_PROPERTY, "on"));
+    }
+
     public void writeToLog(SimulationModel model, String outputPathWithoutExtension) throws IOException {
 
+        if (isDisabled()) {
+            return;
+        }
+
         Map<String, ProcessSimulationComponents> desmojObjectsMap = model.getDesmojObjectsMap();
         for (String processId : desmojObjectsMap.keySet()) {
             String fileNameWithoutExtension = model.getDesmojObjectsMap().get(processId).getCommonProcessElements()
